WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:10.030
52. Northern Lights The beautiful northern lights sweep across

2
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:16.210
the northern skies. Sometimes they look like blue or green smoke. Sometimes they look like

3
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.610
a vast white scarf shaken out between the stars. They appear mysteriously, as if from

4
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:28.890
another world, and they have been inspiring mankind for centuries. The Cree people called

5
00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:34.190
them the Dance of the Spirits. Some ancient Norse thought the lights were reflections

6
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.570
off the shields of fallen ancient soldiers going to their paradise. Others thought they

7
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:46.130
were oceans surrounded by fire. The red lights can also look like a breath of fire from a

8
00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:52.890
dragon. In fact, they may be a source of dragon myths. Red lights were often thought to predict

9
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:58.490
wars. Some cultures hide when the northern lights are in the sky. Others watch them with

10
00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:05.210
respect. Many Asian cultures believe children born under northern lights will be lucky,

11
00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:11.850
but some European cultures believe the opposite. These mysterious lights that inspire our imaginations

12
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:18.170
really do come from another world. They come from the sun. The northern lights, or aurora

13
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.730
borealis, their scientific name, result from solar wind connecting with particles high

14
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:30.330
in Earth's atmosphere. This connection causes the particles to give off different substances. When

15
00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:36.690
there are storms on the sun, we see more auroras because there's more solar wind. The different

16
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:43.450
colors of the auroras are a result of different particles release different substances. All this

17
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:50.330
activity can cause problems for radios and other electronic tools, though it creates unbelievable

18
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:56.130
art in the sky. The northern lights are still a source of inspiration for human beings.

19
00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:04.330
Photographers, painters, writers, they all try to capture the awe that these lights create. However,

20
00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:10.050
these lights are difficult to pin down on paper. You may just have to see them for yourself.
